librespot
  https://github.com/librespot-org/librespot
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2015 Paul Lietar, and its contributors.
  An open source Spotify client library. Its source is where the client id
  that the "Keymaster" sign-in option uses (KEYMASTER_CLIENT_ID in
  core/src/config.rs) was found. That is a single public identifier, not a
  copy of any of its code.

spotifyd
  https://github.com/Spotifyd/spotifyd
  GNU General Public License v3.0.
  A Spotify Connect daemon built on librespot. Its sign-in flow is where the
  loopback redirect used by the "Keymaster" option (127.0.0.1:8000/login)
  was observed. The optional local player installs it with Homebrew and runs
  it as a separate program (a LaunchAgent): it builds its command line,
  reads its log and stops it, but includes, copies, links to and modifies
  none of its code. Whether that leaves this package outside the GPL is for
  you to judge; this is not legal advice.

Thanks to the authors and maintainers of both projects for the years of work
that made playing Spotify from the terminal practical.
